## cloud@hetzner.hetzbot · grove_provision_5_4_gh_configure_upsert
rc=1
   ✋ ConstraintError: gh is unauthed, and the rack holds no 'GITHUB_TOKEN' to give it
      ⇒ this box is 'cloud@hetzner.hetzbot'; only 'local@unix' confirms a
        human at a keyboard, so no login prompt may open here
      ⇒ a login prompt is deliberately NOT opened: a duct is tmux, so
        the question would sit on the pane and then consume the next
        command sent down the duct as its answer
      ⇒ until a token lands, every github reach fails on auth: the org
        clone, the issue read, the pr open — most of what a grove does

      🙋 A HUMAN IS OWED HERE — run this ON THIS BOX, from the checkout:

        cd ~/git/more/dev-env-setup && rhx keyrack set \
          --owner ehmpath --key GITHUB_TOKEN \
          --org @all --env camp --vault os.secure

      it asks two questions, in this order:
        1. which mechanism?  → 1 (PERMANENT_VIA_REPLICA)
        2. enter secret      → paste the pat

      ⚠️ ANSWER BOTH AT THE PROMPTS. do not pipe them in: the secret
         prompt masks its echo, so it reads the terminal, not stdin. fed
         a pipe, set takes the mechanism answer, SKIPS the secret, stores
         an EMPTY value, and prints '✔ set' regardless — and the blank
         only surfaces later, as a token github rejects

      ⚠️ there is NO second 'keyrack fill' step. set stores the value
         itself; fill re-drives the very same prompts, so a set-then-fill
         chain sends the pat into fill's FIRST question — which asks for
         a mechanism — and keyrack rejects it with expected: "1-2".

      the value is never an argument, so it reaches neither 'ps' nor the
      shell history; keyrack writes it encrypted, in the vault named above

      mint the pat at https://github.com/settings/tokens with 'repo' +
      'read:org'. see grove.auth.github.roadmap.md — the pat is phase 1,
      and phase 2 replaces it with a per-org app token that mints itself

## cloud@hetzner.hetzbot · grove_provision_5_4_gh_configure_verify
rc=1
   ✋ ConstraintError: gh holds no credential github will accept
      ⇒ a SET GH_TOKEN is not enough: an expired or under-scoped token
        passes a presence test and fails at the first api call, inside
        whichever skill made it — never here
      ⇒ so this asks github, and github said no
      fix (this box confirms no human, so a login cannot be answered):
        1. cd ~/git/more/dev-env-setup && rhx keyrack set \
             --owner ehmpath --key GITHUB_TOKEN \
             --org @all --env camp --vault os.secure
           answer its two prompts: mechanism 1, then paste the pat
      ⚠️ the pat needs BOTH scopes: 'repo' to clone, 'read:org' so gh
         can enumerate. one with only 'repo' clones every repo you
         name and cannot tell you what there is to name
        2. rhx grove.provision --what 5.4.gh --mode apply
      ⚠️ step 2 is NOT optional after a scope change on the same pat.
         git asks the rack on every fetch, so it picks a rescope up at
         once. gh holds a STORED LOGIN taken here, so its copy stays
         stale until this bundle re-reads the rack. measured 2026-08-05:
         git went green on a rescoped pat while gh stayed refused
      the value is typed on a tty and stored encrypted by its vault — never pass
      it as an argument, and never export it into a duct pane
      ⚠️ one set, no fill: set stores the value itself, and fill re-drives
         its prompts, so a chained fill takes the pat as a mechanism answer
      see grove.auth.github.roadmap.md
      read why: gh auth status

